<mxCell id="p2-v35" parent="p2-v34" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;fontColor=#0F172A;fontFamily=Arial;" value="• Command, so dedupe on event_id.&lt;br&gt;• The cursor is saved with each page, so a restart resumes and the unique message row stops a double send.&lt;br&gt;• Senders are LLD 15, in the marketing pool. The send variant is LLD 7." vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="16" y="44" width="378" height="344" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="p2-v36" parent="1" style="swimlane;startSize=32;rounded=1;arcSize=8;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;align=left;spacingLeft=12;fillColor=#F8FAFC;strokeColor=#64748B;swimlaneFillColor=#F8FAFC;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0F172A;" value="Notes  ·  decisions cited" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="1484" y="544" width="460" height="400" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="p2-v37" parent="p2-v36" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;fontColor=#0F172A;fontFamily=Arial;" value="• ponytail: the message log is the send queue. Workers claim rows in status queued. Ceiling: row churn on a multi-million broadcast. Upgrade: SQS per priority lane, same workers.&lt;br&gt;• Transactional messages never wait for quiet hours.&lt;br&gt;• Campaign reads stats over gRPC (LLD 13). There is no fact out." vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="16" y="44" width="428" height="344" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
