<mxCell id="lld-14-n31" parent="1" style="swimlane;startSize=32;rounded=1;arcSize=8;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;align=left;spacingLeft=12;fillColor=#F8FAFC;strokeColor=#64748B;swimlaneFillColor=#F8FAFC;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0F172A;" value="Contract  ·  fields (draft)" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="16" y="544" width="600" height="400" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="lld-14-n32" parent="lld-14-n31" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;fontColor=#0F172A;fontFamily=Courier New;" value="worker claims messages where status = queued and due_at &lt;= now&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;pool is pinned: a worker serves one pool&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;push: one row, every live device&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;any 200 → sent&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;token invalid → devices.invalid_at&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;every token invalid → failed&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;inbox: insert inbox_items, no HTTP&lt;br&gt;frame: PUBLISH ws:{brand}:{customer}&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;publish failure leaves the row sent" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="16" y="44" width="568" height="344" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="lld-14-n33" parent="1" style="swimlane;startSize=32;rounded=1;arcSize=8;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;align=left;spacingLeft=12;fillColor=#F8FAFC;strokeColor=#64748B;swimlaneFillColor=#F8FAFC;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0F172A;" value="Writes  ·  tables" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="632" y="544" width="410" height="400" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="lld-14-n34" parent="lld-14-n33" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;fontColor=#0F172A;fontFamily=Courier New;" value="messages.status&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;queued → sent | failed | skipped&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;provider_message_id on sent&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;attempts&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;inbox_items  when channel = inbox&lt;br&gt;devices.invalid_at  on a bad FCM token&lt;br&gt;the row stays; status is the record" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="16" y="44" width="378" height="344" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="lld-14-n35" parent="1" style="swimlane;startSize=32;rounded=1;arcSize=8;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;align=left;spacingLeft=12;fillColor=#F8FAFC;strokeColor=#64748B;swimlaneFillColor=#F8FAFC;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0F172A;" value="Dedupe  ·  deadline  ·  retry" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="1058" y="544" width="410" height="400" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="lld-14-n36" parent="lld-14-n35" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;fontColor=#0F172A;fontFamily=Arial;" value="• Provider 5xx: 3 tries with backoff, then failed. 4xx other than an invalid token fails immediately.&lt;br&gt;• A crash after the provider 200 and before our commit can send one duplicate. The unique row stops a Kafka replay, not this.&lt;br&gt;• Rate limit is a Valkey token bucket per brand and provider. An empty bucket leaves the row queued." vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="16" y="44" width="378" height="344" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="lld-14-n37" parent="1" style="swimlane;startSize=32;rounded=1;arcSize=8;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;align=left;spacingLeft=12;fillColor=#F8FAFC;strokeColor=#64748B;swimlaneFillColor=#F8FAFC;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0F172A;" value="Notes  ·  decisions cited" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="1484" y="544" width="460" height="400" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="lld-14-n38" parent="lld-14-n37" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;fontColor=#0F172A;fontFamily=Arial;" value="• OTP, transactional, and marketing never share a worker. A broadcast cannot delay a code.&lt;br&gt;• Quiet hours are 21:00–08:00, marketing only. The frequency cap number is a draft.&lt;br&gt;• No personal data is written. The contact is used for the HTTP call and dropped.&lt;br&gt;• LINE unfollow (LLD 4) sets line_blocked, and this worker then skips LINE." vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="16" y="44" width="428" height="344" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
</root></mxGraphModel></diagram>
<diagram name="16 · UnregisterDevice" id="lld-15"><mxGraphModel dx="1980" dy="960" grid="1" gridSize="8" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1980" pageHeight="960" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="0" /><mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
<mxCell id="lld-15-n1" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=22;fontColor=#0F172A;fontFamily=Arial;fontStyle=1;" value="Notification LLD 16 — UnregisterDevice: logout marks the push token invalid" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="24" y="12" width="1920" height="32" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="lld-15-n2" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#64748B;fontFamily=Arial;" value="Draft with the app team on the trigger. When logout calls UnregisterDevice, the token is marked invalid so the next push skips that phone. RegisterDevice on the same token (LLD 5) clears it.  Draft LLD: field names and status values are to be aligned with the business." vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="24" y="46" width="1920" height="34" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
